{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02856",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 7.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.59,
      "end_seconds": 13.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.17,
      "end_seconds": 21.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "Doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.58,
      "end_seconds": 27.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 28.16,
      "end_seconds": 37.65,
      "duration_seconds": 9.49,
      "text": "Oh, it's a severe sore throat on one side, doctor. He didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.09,
      "end_seconds": 42.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.34,
      "end_seconds": 48.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "A eight out of ten, uh, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.6,
      "end_seconds": 52.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Is it worse at certain times?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.17,
      "end_seconds": 57.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Erm, swallowing definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.99,
      "end_seconds": 66.42,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 66.52,
      "end_seconds": 72.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.51,
      "end_seconds": 76.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.81,
      "end_seconds": 81.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "What about a muffled voice, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.38,
      "end_seconds": 88.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Yes, I have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.8,
      "end_seconds": 90.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Any drooling as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.47,
      "end_seconds": 95.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Okay, so yes, for six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 96.08,
      "end_seconds": 99.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Yes, that's right, that's how it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 102.54,
      "end_seconds": 111.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 39.2 degrees, pressure 118 over 68, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, heart rate 97."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.59,
      "end_seconds": 113.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.54,
      "end_seconds": 117.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.76,
      "end_seconds": 122.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.29,
      "end_seconds": 124.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.43,
      "end_seconds": 151.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "The right tonsil is pushed towards the middle, the uvula is deviated, and the palate is swollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.16,
      "end_seconds": 154.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.59,
      "end_seconds": 164.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So, and what about rash, noisy breathing or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.17,
      "end_seconds": 180.79,
      "duration_seconds": 14.62,
      "text": "No, no rash, no noisy breathing, no cough. I did have difficulty opening my mouth at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.13,
      "end_seconds": 184.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.34,
      "end_seconds": 188.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.53,
      "end_seconds": 198.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "So, what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.01,
      "end_seconds": 206.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 208.16,
      "end_seconds": 217.64,
      "duration_seconds": 9.48,
      "text": "He is supposed to take it twice a day, but I can't say he always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.06,
      "end_seconds": 224.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.59,
      "end_seconds": 239.41,
      "duration_seconds": 12.82,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. No, I've never smoked in my life. No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.51,
      "end_seconds": 256.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.66,
      "end_seconds": 262.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Just keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.68,
      "end_seconds": 285.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.55,
      "end_seconds": 291.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Ah, I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 296.9,
      "end_seconds": 304.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "I mean, hold on, doctor, I think he reacted to diclofenac once. I'm not certain, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.71,
      "end_seconds": 308.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.36,
      "end_seconds": 316.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.29,
      "end_seconds": 321.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Arthritis in my knees, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.34,
      "end_seconds": 327.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "And besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.27,
      "end_seconds": 333.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.24,
      "end_seconds": 368.23,
      "duration_seconds": 32.99,
      "text": "Alright, arthritis in your knees and high blood pressure, that matches what I have here. Putting it all together, I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at a quinsy, a peritonsillar abscess or severe tonsillitis. We should do blood tests for abscess. Let's get an urgent ENT drainage, for peritonsillar abscess. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.32,
      "end_seconds": 373.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "How long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.89,
      "end_seconds": 412.74,
      "duration_seconds": 37.85,
      "text": "We'll begin with benzylpenicillin, 1.2 grams, now, single dose. That should help with peritonsillar abscess. You need to be seen by ENT today to drain it. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. Do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse. Let's review you straight away. Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.78,
      "end_seconds": 424.63,
      "duration_seconds": 9.85,
      "text": "So, I take the benzylpenicillin, 1.2 grams, now and come back straight away. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 426.7,
      "end_seconds": 431.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. So, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.33,
      "end_seconds": 438.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Okay, um, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}